{
  "id": "grammar.a2.imperfecto1.03.irregulares",
  "title": "Imperfecto Irregulars: ser, ir, ver",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "Only three verbs are irregular in the imperfecto. All other verbs — even those irregular in the present or preterite — are completely regular in the imperfecto."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "ser (to be)",
      "rows": [
        [
          "yo",
          "era"
        ],
        [
          "tú",
          "eras"
        ],
        [
          "él/ella/usted",
          "era"
        ],
        [
          "nosotros",
          "éramos"
        ],
        [
          "ellos/ustedes",
          "eran"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "ir (to go)",
      "rows": [
        [
          "yo",
          "iba"
        ],
        [
          "tú",
          "ibas"
        ],
        [
          "él/ella/usted",
          "iba"
        ],
        [
          "nosotros",
          "íbamos"
        ],
        [
          "ellos/ustedes",
          "iban"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "ver (to see / to watch)",
      "rows": [
        [
          "yo",
          "veía"
        ],
        [
          "tú",
          "veías"
        ],
        [
          "él/ella/usted",
          "veía"
        ],
        [
          "nosotros",
          "veíamos"
        ],
        [
          "ellos/ustedes",
          "veían"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "es": "De niño, era muy tímido.",
          "en": "As a child, I was very shy."
        },
        {
          "es": "Ibamos al parque todos los sábados.",
          "en": "We used to go to the park every Saturday."
        },
        {
          "es": "Ella veía la televisión por las noches.",
          "en": "She used to watch TV at night."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "Notice: ver follows -ER endings (-ía), ir is unique (-iba), and ser is completely irregular (era). Memorise all three paradigms separately."
    }
  ]
}